 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The loading time is proportional to the file size and the complexity of the compression format (gzip or ZSTD) [S2, unofficial]. The asynchronous nature ensures the main thread remains responsive.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of splats, storing positions, covariances, colors, and SH coefficients [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Non-blocking I/O prevents UI freezes; supports multiple compression formats [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires careful management of the callback lifecycle to avoid dangling references; memory usage can be high for very large scenes [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Asynchronous loading time depends on I/O speed and file size (`.spz`/`.ply` parsing). The `start` call is $O(1)$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N \cdot C)$, where $N$ is the number of splats and $C$ is the number of SH coefficients per splat. The SH data is packed tightly into `RGBA16F` texels [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Non-blocking UI/main thread; efficient GPU memory layout for SH coefficients [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Requires a callback-based architecture; error handling is string-based [S1, unofficial].
+*   **When to use:** Real-time applications requiring smooth frame rates during asset loading [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-The `ISplatSource` interface was introduced in the `splat-ros/RVizSplat` project to facilitate real-time visualization of 3D Gaussian Splatting data in ROS environments [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the performance bottlenecks associated with synchronous loading of large-scale splat captures.
+The `ISplatSource` interface originates from the `splat-ros/RVizSplat` project, an unofficial implementation for integrating 3D Gaussian Splatting into ROS-based visualization tools [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address the performance bottlenecks of synchronous splat loading in interactive 3D environments.
 
